<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/7th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Revolution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Xuanwu Gate Incident</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">626 CE</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Xuanwu Gate Incident was a palace coup in 626 CE in which <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-taizong-of-tang">Li Shimin</a> ambushed and killed his brothers, the crown prince <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/li-jiancheng">Li Jiancheng</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/li-yuanji">Li Yuanji</a>, at the Xuanwu Gate of the Tang palace in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/changan">Chang'an</a>. His father, Emperor Gaozu, soon abdicated in his favour. Li Shimin then reigned as Emperor Taizong, one of the most celebrated rulers of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tang-dynasty">Tang Dynasty</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/xuanwu-gate-incident.jpg" alt="Xuanwu Gate Incident" width="203" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown artistUnknown artist · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:TangTaizong.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
